      "component_id": "ED26-P15-CH-measurable-probability-C016",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "Durrett's extended random variable (p. 17) is defined on a set D in F, takes values in R*=[-inf,inf] with the Borel sets of its usual topology generated by [-inf,a), (a,b), (b,inf]; his almost sure convergence (pp. 16-17) means P(Omega_o)=1 for Omega_o={lim X_n exists}, with no prescribed limit, and he sets X_inf = limsup X_n. The entry requires all of Omega as domain, uses the sigma-algebra generated by [-inf,a], and defines almost sure convergence only to a specified real X; none of the source forms or their relation to the entry's forms is on the route, although later chapters say 'converges almost surely' without a prescribed limit. Supply the variants and prove the bridges.",
